        {
          "id": 3081713732,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "I think explaining that the commit failed is a good step - a couple of times it has failed and I didn't even noticed immediately.  What I really want is the chance to fix my commit message - a couple of times now I've typed in quite detailed descriptions, had them rejected/lost and typed in a terse 1-line description the 2nd time around.\n\nI do realise I could fish them out of .git/COMMIT_EDITMSG, or even use commit --edit --file...",
